ationViewSet.get_queryset hides expired and legacy tokens (404)."},{"path":"taiga/projects/services/members.py","summary":"Bulk invitations get the token and expiration date from generate_invitation_token; removed unused uuid import."},{"path":"taiga/export_import/services/store.py","summary":"Imported memberships get the token and expiration date through set_invitation_token, so an expiration date from the dump is overwritten; removed unused uuid import."},{"path":"taiga/projects/management/commands/sample_data.py","summary":"Sample invitations use generate_invitation_token."},{"path":"taiga/projects/validators.py","summary":"MembershipValidator: token and token_expires_at are read-only, so clients cannot choose a token or its expiration date."},{"path":"tests/factories.py","summary":"MembershipFactory and InvitationFactory set token_expires_at to now + 7 days."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_auth.py","summary":"Tests: login with an expired or legacy invitation_token returns 404 and does not accept the invitation; private registration works with a valid token and returns 404 with an expired or legacy one (no user is created)."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_memberships.py","summary":"Tests: the helper returns a unique token valid for 7 days; API create, bulk create and get_members_from_bulk set the expiration date; client-supplied token and date are ignored; resend rotates the token and the old token returns 404; get invitation by valid, expired or legacy token."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_importer_api.py","summary":"Test: project import gives invitations a fresh token valid for 7 days and ignores the expiration date in the dump."}],"acceptance":[{"criterion":"Every issuer sets the token and its expiration date together through one shared helper","met":true,"evidence":"grep shows no remaining direct uuid token assignment for memberships; API create, bulk create, import and sample_data all use generate_invitation_token or set_invitation_token. Tests cover API create, bulk create and import."},{"criterion":"Expired and legacy tokens are rejected everywhere (GET invitation by token, login, register)","met":true,"evidence":"Parametrized tests (expired and None) for GET /invitations/<token> (404), login with invitation_token (404, membership.user stays None) and private registration (404, no user created): all pass."},{"criterion":"Resending rotates the token and refreshes the expiration date","met":true,"evidence":"test_api_resend_invitation_rotates_token: a new token valid for 7 days, the email contains the new token, the old token returns 404 and the new one returns 200."},{"criterion":"Factories create invitations valid for one week","met":true,"evidence":"tests/factories.py: token_expires_at = timezone.now() + timedelta(days=7) on MembershipFactory and InvitationFactory."},{"criterion":"Change is covered by tests","met":true,"evidence":"41 selected tests (new and related) pass in test_auth.py, test_memberships.py and test_importer_api.py."},{"criterion":"Existing test suite still passes","met":false,"evidence":"Related integration files (test_auth, test_memberships, test_projects, test_users) pass: 278 passed. The full `pytest tests` run was started in the background but had not finished when this report was written, so the whole suite is not confirmed. No model changed, so no migration was needed."}],"human_needed":[{"question":"Is it OK that API clients can no longer set `token` and `token_expires_at` on memberships (they are now read-only in MembershipValidator)?","why":"Before, a client could choose its own invitation token, and that token would have no expiration date. The existing permission test sends token='test' on PUT and still passes, but a frontend that relies on writing these fields would be affected."},{"question":"Should existing pending invitations get a migration that sets an expiration date, instead of being treated as expired?","why":"The task says legacy tokens are treated as expired, so all invi